### =====================================================================
### POC 2: Embeddings and similarity. Requests in learning order.
###
### HOW TO USE
###   1. Start the app (Eclipse: run TutorApplication, or java -jar tutor/target/tutor.jar).
###      Ollama must be running with nomic-embed-text (check: ollama list).
###   2. Open this file in one of these:
###        - IntelliJ IDEA (built-in HTTP Client): click the green arrow next to a request
###        - VS Code + "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above a request
###      Eclipse has no .http runner. Use Swagger (http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html)
###      with the same values, or copy the URL into a browser (all requests are GET).
###   3. Run the requests TOP TO BOTTOM. Each one builds on the one before.
###      Before moving on, read the "Observe" line and say the takeaway in one sentence.
###
### NOTES
###   - "+" in a URL means a space. "%3F" means "?".
###   - The first request that uses the 15 test sentences takes about 1 s more: it embeds them once.
### =====================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 1 (POC 2.1): What is an embedding?
### Observe: 768 numbers, vectorLength ~1.0, ~90 ms (a chat answer takes ~5 s).
### Takeaway: text becomes numbers. One number alone means nothing.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/embed?text=An+AI+agent+uses+tools+to+complete+tasks.

### STEP 1b: a completely different text. The numbers look just as random.
GET {{host}}/poc02/embed?text=Pasta+needs+boiling+salted+water.


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 2 (POC 2.1): Compare two texts with cosine similarity
### Observe: the hand-written cosine equals LangChain4j's (0.6759).
### Takeaway: cosine = "do the two vectors point the same way?" Higher = closer meaning.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/similarity

### STEP 2b: similar meaning, different words. Expect a fairly high score.
GET {{host}}/poc02/similarity?a=I+love+cricket&b=I+enjoy+playing+sports

### STEP 2c: unrelated. Expect lower, but NOT zero.
GET {{host}}/poc02/similarity?a=I+love+cricket&b=Pasta+needs+boiling+salted+water.

### STEP 2d: same words, opposite meaning. Does the model notice the "not"?
GET {{host}}/poc02/similarity?a=The+movie+was+good&b=The+movie+was+not+good


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 3 (POC 2.1): Hand-picked pairs, including a surprise
### Observe: "Java" language vs "Java" island = 0.745, HIGHER than real synonyms (0.676).
### Takeaway: embeddings capture meaning well, but not perfectly. Shared words still pull scores up.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/pairs


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 4 (POC 2.2): Every sentence against every other sentence
### Observe: the "Score range" line at the bottom: min ~0.29, mean ~0.45, max ~0.75.
### Takeaway: even unrelated texts score ~0.3, so "0.5 = similar" means nothing.
###           Only the RANKING counts (and each model has its own range).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/matrix


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 5 (POC 2.3): Semantic search vs keyword search (THE key lesson)
### Observe: compare "semantic" with "keyword" in each answer.
### Takeaway: keyword search matches words; semantic search matches meaning.
###           This is why RAG (POC 3) uses embeddings.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a: semantic search also finds "I drink a cup of java"; keyword search finds only "coffee beans".
GET {{host}}/poc02/search?query=coffee&k=3

### 5b: keyword search finds NOTHING ("autonomously" is not "autonomous").
GET {{host}}/poc02/search?query=software+that+works+autonomously&k=3

### 5c: semantic search finds both islands; keyword search finds only Bali.
GET {{host}}/poc02/search?query=holiday+destinations&k=3

### 5d: semantic search finds vector database, RAG and embeddings; keyword search matches only "text".
GET {{host}}/poc02/search?query=how+do+I+find+similar+text%3F&k=3

### 5e: your turn. Ask with words that appear in NO sentence.
GET {{host}}/poc02/search?query=tasty+Italian+dinner&k=3


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 6 (POC 2.4): Break it: nomic's task prefixes
### Observe: with prefixes, S3 scores 0.762 (vs 0.658 without), and "Java island" drops from #2 to #3.
### Takeaway: HOW you embed changes WHAT you find. Read the model card.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/prefixes

### 6b: another question. Does the ranking change between the two lists?
GET {{host}}/poc02/prefixes?query=What+is+an+AI+agent%3F&k=5


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP 7 (POC 2.5): Architect numbers (cost and storage)
### Observe: batchTotalMs < oneByOneTotalMs; bytesPerVector = 3072; storage for 1M vectors ~3 GB.
### Takeaway: the numbers a customer asks about. They go into
###           docs/artifacts/poc02-choosing-embedding-model.md
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/poc02/embedding-stats
